SUMMARY:Revolutionary Text Series No. 3
DESCRIPTION:George Washington’s Letter to the Hebrew Congregation of\nNewport\, Rhode Island\, 1790\nSunday\, October 11th | 11:45 Parish House Forum Room\nJoin Professor Randall Zachman to explore the thinking behind George Washington’s 1790 letter to the Jewish congregation in Newport\, Rhode Island\, in which he wrote that the new nation gives no sanction to bigotry nor assistance to persecution. Today\, the letter is considered a stepping stone for the First Amendment that would come the following year. \nRegistration is required for catering with a suggested donation of $25 for adults. \nRegistration deadline: Monday\, October 5th. \nClick here to register.
URL:https://www.saintjameslancaster.org/event/revolutionary-text-series-no-3/
LOCATION:Saint James Parish House\, 119 North Duke Street\, Lancaster\, PA\, 17602\, United States
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.saintjameslancaster.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/Revolutionary-Text-2-copy.jpg
GEO:40.0404103;-76.303616
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=Saint James Parish House 119 North Duke Street Lancaster PA 17602 United States;X-APPLE-RADIUS=500;X-TITLE=119 North Duke Street:geo:-76.303616,40.0404103
END:VEVENT
